# Supabase configuration
# Local dev now runs the Worker itself via `wrangler dev` (see "dev:api" in
# package.json), which reads its secrets from `.dev.vars` (git-ignored) in
# the repo root, not from this file. Copy the values below into `.dev.vars`.
SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"

# SECRET -- bypasses all row-level security. Never commit a real value.
# Preferred name: SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY. The Worker reads
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY ?? SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, so the legacy name still
# works but SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY should be used for anything new.
# Local dev: put it in .dev.vars (git-ignored), read by `wrangler dev`.
# Deployment: set it through the Cloudflare dashboard -- see DEPLOY.md,
# section 2 ("Environment and secrets") -- never with `wrangler secret put`.
# Never place it in wrangler.toml [vars] -- that block is plaintext.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY="your-secret-key"

# Cloudflare / frontend configuration
# Set this when the frontend is served from Cloudflare Pages and the API sits on a separate domain.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=""

# Optional runtime limits
MAX_LISTINGS_PER_USER="20"

# ============================================================================
# DESTRUCTIVE. THIS IS ALREADY "true" FOR LOCAL `wrangler dev` (inherited from
# wrangler.toml [vars] -- see below). ONLY SET IT TO "false" BELOW IF YOU WANT
# TO DISABLE IT LOCALLY.
# ============================================================================
#
# Setting this to "true" makes the Worker's daily cron sweep find every
# FINISHED listing (sold, cancelled, admin-hidden, or expired) whose
# expires_at is more than 30 days in the past and PERMANENTLY DELETE its
# photos -- it sets image_url to null and image_urls to an empty array. A
# live listing always has expires_at in the future, so it can never match
# and is never touched, no matter how old -- see cleanupStaleImages in
# workers/shared.ts.
#
# This CANNOT BE UNDONE. Listing images are stored as base64 inside Postgres,
# so the row is the only copy of the photo. There is no object store holding a
# second copy and there is no backup.
#
# Worse: SUPABASE_URL above is the same project in .dev.vars and wrangler.toml.
# There is no separate development database. Turning this on for a local
# `wrangler dev` session deletes photos from listings that real people are
# looking at.
#
# `wrangler.toml` sets this to "true" in [vars], and `wrangler dev` inherits
# [vars] as its starting environment -- so leaving this line commented out
# does NOT disable the sweep locally, it just lets the wrangler.toml value
# through. To disable it for local `wrangler dev`, uncomment the line below
# with "false": .dev.vars overrides [vars] for `wrangler dev`, so this local
# override takes precedence over wrangler.toml regardless of what the deployed
# Worker uses in production.
#
# ENABLE_STALE_IMAGE_CLEANUP="false"
